Agent / tool use:

- Terminal-Bench / Tau-Bench / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas / SWE Atlas: **no verified public score found** — only qualitative community reports of "exceptional tool-use consistency … without getting caught in circular retry loops" (kie.ai; r/LocalLLaMA). No reproducible numbers.

Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond / HLE / LCR / MLCR / CritPt: **no verified public score found**.
- Artificial Analysis Intelligence Index: **not tracked** — `artificialanalysis.ai/models/qoduck` and `/models/lmodel` both return HTTP 404.
- BenchLM overall: **not tracked** — `benchlm.ai/models/qoduck` returns HTTP 404.
- Only claim: an unnamed group ("AI Tracker") reports QoDuck "systematically outperformed all previously released Qwen models" in controlled knowledge evals — no numeric scores, not reproducible, not attributable to a first-party/dedicated host.

Coding:

- SWE-bench Verified / LiveCodeBench / HumanEval / SciCode / Vibe Code Bench: **no verified public score found**. kie.ai states explicitly: "no formal, reproducible benchmark results (such as SWE-bench or HumanEval scores) have been released."
- Only anecdote: a head-to-head refactoring timing (QoDuck 40 min vs DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash 70 min) in unspecified user trials — a wall-clock anecdote, not a scored benchmark.

Long context:

- 1,000,000-token window confirmed via client catalog data, but **no long-context retrieval benchmark reported** (no MRCR / RULER / GraphWalks score).

Multimodal:

- Image/vision input "observed" by community testing (partially confirmed), text + code output; **no multimodal benchmark score found**, and the vendor has not confirmed image support.

> Provenance & meta verification:
> - `model/qoduck/meta.json` is a scaffolded stub (`"scaffolded": true`): it claims "128K total" context and "Text in/out". Both are CONTRADICTED by the Qoder client catalog (1M window) and community testing (code-first, observed multimodal). Premise-corrected above on the fresh vendor/community evidence — recommend the orchestrator regenerate this stub.
> - Lineage: tokenizer fingerprint matches the Qwen 3.8 vocabulary (AI Tracker via kie.ai). Widely speculated to preview an unreleased Qwen checkpoint (a "Qwen 4" branch), but Alibaba has NOT confirmed generation or parameter scale — treat lineage as unconfirmed.

